  GUARD  is this aimaxes's instrument?  F1 swing 363.6 against its 378.3,
         F1 rest 626.9 against its 629.7   -> OK

  6 TEACHABLE AXES QUALIFY, against aimaxes's 2, for a code space of
  1144.0 signals with NO new learning rule. BUT THIS IS NOT A WORD COUNT
  AND MAY NOT BE QUOTED AS ONE: the ear is the gate, not the larynx, and
  whether it RESOLVES the new axes is unmeasured -- kVLScoreFormant scores
  only F1/F2. Stage two is that measurement, and §41 forbids a naming
  claim until it exists.

  AND §41's OWN POWER ARGUMENT WAS WRONG, WHICH IS WORTH MORE THAN THE
  RESULT. It named CROSS-TALK as "the cheapest thing that could refuse
  this". It could not: the groups are DISJOINT INDEX SLICES and each
  parameter is a centroid over its own slice, so a ramp inside one slice
  can only reach another through lateral dynamics -- near-zero was
  structurally near-certain, and a bar of 0.10 against measured 0.007 was
  never going to bind. The clause that actually did work was CLAUSE 1,
  which caught the two readouts this instrument cannot drive at all. A
  pre-registered refusal clause is only as good as its chance of firing.
